    <evidenceRef id="caf:concept:evidence:example-dependency-repair:source" kind="source" ref="caf:concept:model:reflaxe-elixir:example-dependency-repair" role="proposal-source" authority="authored">This declaration records the requested selection, not a successful installation.</evidenceRef>
    <fallbackJustification id="caf:concept:fallback:example-dependency-repair" result="partial-gap-after-reuse" reviewedTargetRefs={["caf:agentspec:rule:dependency-integration-lifecycle"]} evidenceRefs={["caf:concept:evidence:example-dependency-repair:source"]}>Reuse native Mix installation and the existing dependency lifecycle. Concept markup supplies the missing explanation; no new installer is needed.</fallbackJustification>
    <anchor id="caf:concept:anchor:example-dependency-repair:servers" name="Example servers" role="boundary" boundary="These examples have native runtime dependencies separate from the compiler release tools." targetRefs={[]} evidenceRefs={[]}>Phoenix examples use Bandit for HTTP. Database examples also use Decimal through Ecto. Mailer examples use idna through Swoosh. LiveView examples use phoenix_live_view. Phoenix examples use Phoenix Presence and channel broadcasts.</anchor>
    <statement id="caf:concept:statement:example-dependency-repair:selection" kind="intent" subjectAnchorRefs={["caf:concept:anchor:example-dependency-repair:servers"]} targetRefs={[]} evidenceRefs={["caf:concept:evidence:example-dependency-repair:source"]} claimBoundary="A selected version is not proof that the examples pass." detailMarkdown="[Bandit 1.14.1](https://hex.pm/packages/bandit/1.14.1) ([changelog](https://github.com/mtrudel/bandit/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)), [Bandit 1.13.1](https://hex.pm/packages/bandit/1.13.1), [Decimal 3.1.2](https://hex.pm/packages/decimal/3.1.2), [Swoosh 1.30.0](https://hex.pm/packages/swoosh/1.30.0), [idna 8.0.0](https://hex.pm/packages/idna/8.0.0), [phoenix_live_view 1.2.14](https://hex.pm/packages/phoenix_live_view/1.2.14), [phoenix 1.7.25](https://hex.pm/packages/phoenix/1.7.25), [phoenix 1.8.17](https://hex.pm/packages/phoenix/1.8.17). [Request authority advisory](https://cna.erlef.org/cves/CVE-2026-105660.html), [HTTP/2 advisory](https://cna.erlef.org/cves/CVE-2026-105659.html), [Decimal advisory](https://cna.erlef.org/cves/CVE-2026-97853.html), [idna advisory](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/EEF-CVE-2026-117678), [LiveView advisory](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/EEF-CVE-2026-126334), [Presence key advisory](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/EEF-CVE-2026-128361), [V1 serializer advisory](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/EEF-CVE-2026-129344). [Parser-error compatibility repair](https://github.com/mtrudel/bandit/pull/719).">Use Bandit 1.14.1 and a supported Decimal release at or above 3.1.2. Update only required dependency constraints and native locks. Keep minimum toolchain and Phoenix behavior intact. Bandit 1.13.0 turned malformed-body errors into HTTP 500 responses. Select 1.13.1 or later to preserve HTTP 400 for malformed JSON and HTTP 413 for oversized bodies. Bandit 1.14.1 fixes the HTTP/1, HTTP/2 and WebSocket advisories that the Hex audit reported for 1.13.1 in November 2026. Use Swoosh 1.30.0 or later and idna 8.0.0 or later: Swoosh releases before 1.30.0 require idna below 8.0.0, and idna releases below 8.0.0 have advisory EEF-CVE-2026-117678. Use phoenix_live_view 1.2.14 or later in the 1.2 line: earlier 1.2 releases have advisory EEF-CVE-2026-126334, where a LiveView join without a URL skips live_session on_mount hooks. Use phoenix 1.7.25 or later in the 1.7 line and phoenix 1.8.17 or later in the 1.8 line: earlier releases have advisories EEF-CVE-2026-128361, where an unsanitized presence key crashes the Presence tracker, and EEF-CVE-2026-129344, where a client-selected V1 serializer crashes shared broadcast dispatch on binary payloads. Phoenix 1.8.17 requires phoenix_pubsub 2.4 or later.</statement>
    <constraint id="caf:concept:constraint:example-dependency-repair:verification" kind="must" appliesToAnchorRefs={["caf:concept:anchor:example-dependency-repair:servers"]} evidenceRefs={[]} boundary="Audit and behavior checks remain independent.">Pass the existing Hex audit without a waiver. Compile the examples and test request handling and decimal rounding through native observers. Keep every required CI check. Exercise parser errors through a real HTTP listener; an in-process connection test cannot detect stale native connection state.</constraint>
    <loweringHint id="caf:concept:lowering:example-dependency-repair:native" kind="use-native-opaque-wrapper" requiredEvidenceRefs={["caf:concept:evidence:example-dependency-repair:source"]}>Use Mix to resolve and install exact upstream packages. Do not patch generated output or dependency source.</loweringHint>
